  "modified": "2026-08-06T16:21:02Z",
  "details": "   * SECURITY UPDATE: fix authentication bypass in cupsd caused by\n     dispatching on the client-supplied Authorization scheme without\n     checking it against the configured AuthType.\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2025-58060.patch: reject \"Authorization: Basic\"\n       unless the effective AuthType is CUPSD_AUTH_BASIC and\n       \"Authorization: Negotiate\" unless it is CUPSD_AUTH_NEGOTIATE in\n       cupsdAuthorize() in scheduler/auth.c.\n     - CVE-2025-58060.\n   * Fix cupsd failing to start with \"cupsdDoSelect() failed - Bad address!\"\n     on hosts whose RLIMIT_NOFILE hard limit is very large but not\n     RLIM_INFINITY, where the epoll event array allocation fails.\n     - debian/patches/maxfds-limit.patch: cap MaxFDs at 65535 in\n       scheduler/main.c, backported from upstream Issue #989.",
